Start with the [documentation index](docs/index.md). Agents: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

- Check everything: `make check` (runs before every push).
- Read the docs as a site: `make docs`.
- See how everything links: `docs/status.md` (each requirement, the code that implements it with file and line,
  and the tests for each scenario) and `docs/links.json` (the same links as data), both rebuilt by `make check`.
- Agents editing code are handed the requirement it implements: `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json`
  run `lockstep-hook` on each edit. Codex runs project hooks only with hooks turned on: add `hooks = true` under
  `[features]` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, then trust the hook when Codex asks.
- The hook also hands over each decision record that governs the file: a `- Governs:` line in
  `docs/decisions/` names paths, folders (ending in `/`) or requirement and capability IDs. A superseded decision is
  flagged. Decisions are in `docs/links.json` too.
- Run one OpenSpec plan with hidden acceptance tests: `uv run lockstep run-plan <change> --agent claude` (or
  `codex`), then merge with `uv run ship` from the worktree it prints. `ship` runs `make check`, refuses a branch
  whose hidden tests failed, and refuses an OpenSpec change that adds a requirement without a decided
  `prior-art.json` (check one with `uv run lockstep check prior-art`).

Needs on the machine: [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), [OpenSpec](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec)
(`openspec`), [lefthook](https://github.com/evilmartians/lefthook), [gitleaks](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks), [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (`npx`, for the diagram check),
[GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/) (`gh`, logged in, for `ship`), Claude Code or Codex (for `run-plan`), and a
git user name and email (global, or answered when the repository was made).

Moved the folder? Run `uv sync --reinstall` once: the Python environment in `.venv` records its folder, so the
commit check cannot start `lockstep` until it is rebuilt. The git hooks themselves move with the folder.
